# TRIM: Trim is the Boolean tool session in its "cut A by B" mode (UE UTrimMeshesTool) - a red 100 cm Box trimmed by a green radius-50 Sphere over its +X top edge previews on the Box (the Sphere hidden), Accept writes it as one undo step, Undo brings both back
Дано run Panel "Open Modeling"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 230,260,300
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.5,-0.45,-0.74
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Box.Width 100
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Box.Depth 100
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Box.Height 100
Дано run Modeling "Create shape tool: Box"
Дано run Modeling "Create shape: place at the viewport centre"
Дано --subject selection set Translation 0,0,0
Дано --subject selection set StaticMeshComponent.MaterialSlots[0] assets:Materials/CB_Red.demat
Дано --subject modeling set CreateShape.Sphere.Radius 50
Дано run Modeling "Create shape tool: Sphere"
Дано run Modeling "Create shape: place at the viewport centre"
Дано --subject selection set Translation 40,60,40
Дано --subject selection set StaticMeshComponent.MaterialSlots[0] assets:Materials/CB_Green.demat
Дано run Modeling "Active tool: Accept"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 150,190,180
Дано run Entity Box
Дано run Entity "Add to selection Sphere"
Дано run Modeling "Trim: Trim A"
Дано run Modeling "Trim: Remove Inside"
Дано run Modeling "Boolean write to: Input"
Дано run Modeling "Boolean inputs: Delete Inputs"
Тогда-вид 0_inputs the red Box with the green Sphere sunk into its near top corner
Когда run Modeling "Boolean tool: Trim"
Тогда 3_trim_preview the red Box with its near top corner cut away by the sphere (an open spherical hole, no green surface); the Sphere hidden; the tool bar at the viewport bottom reads Trim with Accept and Cancel
Когда run Modeling "Active tool: Accept"
Тогда 3_trim_accept the trimmed red Box stays, the Sphere gone from viewport and Outliner; no tool bar
Когда run Action Undo
Тогда 4_trim_undo the whole red Box and the green Sphere in its corner again; Outliner lists both
